IMPORT prelude

-- Price Control Act 1950 (Singapore) -- the offences an ordinary seller or buyer meets when prices are fixed: selling above a
-- fixed maximum price (s 9(1)) and knowingly buying above it (s 9(2)), with the evidence-gathering saving (s 14); the duty to
-- display price lists (ss 7, 8); refusing to sell or falsely denying stock (s 10, with its cash-payment defence); the general
-- penalties (s 16(1), (2)); the debarment order and its breach (s 16(3)); directors' deemed guilt (s 16(4)); and liability for a
-- partner, agent or servant (s 16(6)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PCA1950.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The latest amendment annotated in
-- the body and the Legislative History is Act 15 of 2010 (Criminal Procedure Code 2010, in force 2 January 2011). The ARRANGEMENT
-- OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body by one number (it lists "Short title" against 2); this
-- encoding follows the body's numbering, which also matches the Act's own cross-references (s 2 refers to "section 4" for fixing
-- maximum prices and "section 5(a)" for controlled articles).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: it is the Act under which a maximum price for goods or services can be
-- fixed, and it makes both the seller and a knowing buyer offenders. SCOPED to the provisions a trader or shopper meets. Not
-- encoded: appointments (s 3); the content of price orders (s 4) and controlled-article orders (s 5), whose terms live in
-- subsidiary orders not retrieved; parliamentary control (ss 6, 18(3)-(6)); inspection powers (s 11) and arrest and seizure
-- (s 12) except as offences; obstruction (s 13) beyond a note; attempts and abetment (s 15); evidence and venue (s 16(5), (7));
-- delegation, rules and forms (ss 17-19). No price order is encoded: whether any goods are price-regulated today is not in the
-- deposit.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (the skill itself was not available in
-- this session; the conventions of the finished example rows were followed). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Price Control Act 1950 -- prices`

DECLARE Offender IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body corporate`

§§ `2 and 9 -- selling or buying above the maximum price`

-- s 2: "'sell' ... includes an agreement to sell and an offer to sell, and an offer to sell shall be deemed to include the exposing
-- of goods for sale, the publication of a price list, the furnishing of a quotation ..."; "'selling price' means the actual net
-- price charged to the purchaser of the goods concerned, less all discounts or other allowances".
-- s 9(1): "Any person who sells any price-regulated goods or performs any service at a price which exceeds the maximum price fixed
-- therefor shall be guilty of an offence."
-- s 9(2): "Any person who knowingly purchases or offers to purchase any price-regulated goods or who knowingly pays or offers to pay
-- for a service a charge which exceeds the maximum charge fixed therefor shall be guilty of an offence."
GIVEN `the price charged` IS A NUMBER, `the discounts and allowances` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the selling price` MEANS `the price charged` MINUS `the discounts and allowances`

-- `sold, agreed, offered or exposed for sale` covers every limb of "sell" in s 2.
GIVEN `the goods are price-regulated` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sold, agreed, offered or exposed for sale` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the price charged` IS A NUMBER,
      `the discounts and allowances` IS A NUMBER,
      `the maximum price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `selling above the maximum price is an offence` IF
        `the goods are price-regulated`
    AND `sold, agreed, offered or exposed for sale`
    AND `the selling price` `the price charged` `the discounts and allowances` GREATER THAN `the maximum price`

GIVEN `the goods are price-regulated` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the buyer knew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the price paid or offered` IS A NUMBER,
      `the maximum price` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `buying above the maximum price is an offence` IF
        `the goods are price-regulated`
    AND `the buyer knew`
    AND `the price paid or offered` GREATER THAN `the maximum price`

-- s 14: "No proceedings shall be instituted under this Act against any person duly authorised in that behalf by the Price Controller
-- who has knowingly purchased goods at a price in excess of that fixed ... with the intention of procuring evidence for the purpose
-- of prosecuting the seller".
GIVEN `the goods are price-regulated` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the buyer knew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the price paid or offered` IS A NUMBER,
      `the maximum price` IS A NUMBER,
      `duly authorised by the Price Controller` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intending to procure evidence against the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the buyer may be prosecuted` IF
        `buying above the maximum price is an offence` `the goods are price-regulated` `the buyer knew` `the price paid or offered` `the maximum price`
    AND (NOT (`duly authorised by the Price Controller` AND `intending to procure evidence against the seller`))

§§ `7 and 8 -- displaying prices`

-- s 7: "Any person who deals in any price-regulated goods shall display in English and in any other language ordered by the Price
-- Controller, in a prominent manner and in a conspicuous position so that it can be easily read and is clearly legible to customers
-- ... a list of the current maximum prices ... and any such person who fails to do so shall be guilty of an offence."
GIVEN `deals in price-regulated goods` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a list is displayed in English` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `another language has been ordered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a list is displayed in the ordered language` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prominent, conspicuous and legible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to display the price list is an offence` IF
        `deals in price-regulated goods`
    AND (    (NOT `a list is displayed in English`)
         OR  (`another language has been ordered` AND (NOT `a list is displayed in the ordered language`))
         OR  (NOT `prominent, conspicuous and legible`))

-- s 8: the Price Controller may by Gazette order "require any person who sells by retail any goods or class of goods specified in the
-- order to exhibit clearly and conspicuously ... the price demanded by him ... and any person failing to comply with any such order
-- shall be guilty of an offence." This reaches goods with no fixed maximum, and only RETAIL sellers.
GIVEN `the goods are specified in a display order` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `sells them by retail` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exhibits the price as prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to exhibit a retail price is an offence` IF
        `the goods are specified in a display order`
    AND `sells them by retail`
    AND (NOT `exhibits the price as prescribed`)

§§ `10 -- refusing to sell`

-- s 10: "Any person carrying on a business in the course of which price-regulated goods are normally sold and who has in his
-- possession a stock of such goods, who -- (a) falsely denies that he has those goods in his possession; or (b) refuses, except with
-- the permission of the Price Controller, to sell those goods in reasonable quantities, shall be guilty of an offence: Provided that
-- it shall be a good defence to a charge under paragraph (b) that the accused had reasonable grounds for believing that the purchaser
-- was unable or unwilling to make immediate payment of the price of the goods in cash."
-- The cash defence is to paragraph (b) only; it does not excuse a false denial.
GIVEN `the business normally sells price-regulated goods` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has a stock of them` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `falsely denied having them` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `refused to sell a reasonable quantity` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had the Price Controller's permission` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonably believed the buyer would not pay cash at once` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing to sell is an offence` IF
        `the business normally sells price-regulated goods`
    AND `has a stock of them`
    AND (    `falsely denied having them`
         OR  (    `refused to sell a reasonable quantity`
              AND (NOT `had the Price Controller's permission`)
              AND (NOT `reasonably believed the buyer would not pay cash at once`)))

§§ `16(1), (2) -- general penalties`

-- s 16(1): a person other than a body corporate (but including a director or officer of one), "where no other penalty is specifically
-- provided for such an offence", is liable to "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to
-- both, and in the case of a second or subsequent offence to a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 5 years or to both."
-- s 16(2): a body corporate: "a fine not exceeding $10,000 and in the case of a second or subsequent offence to a fine not exceeding
-- $20,000." No imprisonment is provided for a body corporate (encoded as 0 years).
-- These are the defaults. An order under s 5(h) or a rule under s 18(2)(f) may prescribe its own penalty, capped at s 16 "in
-- corresponding circumstances".
GIVEN `the offender` IS AN Offender, `a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offender`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN IF `a second or subsequent offence` THEN 20000 ELSE 2000
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN IF `a second or subsequent offence` THEN 20000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `the offender` IS AN Offender, `a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offender`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN IF `a second or subsequent offence` THEN 5 ELSE 2
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN 0

§§ `16(3) -- debarment from business`

-- s 16(3): "Where a trader or commission agent is convicted of an offence under this Act the court ... may, in addition to any other
-- penalty, make an order debarring him or any firm of which he is a partner or any corporation of which he is an officer, from
-- carrying on business for such period as the court may determine." Failing to comply: "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or to both."
GIVEN `convicted of an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a trader` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a commission agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may debar from business` IF
    `convicted of an offence under this Act` AND (`is a trader` OR `is a commission agent`)

`the maximum fine for breaching a debarment order` MEANS 20000
`the maximum imprisonment in years for breaching a debarment order` MEANS 1

§§ `16(4) -- directors and officers of a convicted company`

-- s 16(4): where a body corporate is convicted, "every such director or officer shall be deemed to be guilty of that offence unless he
-- proves that the offence was committed without his knowledge or that he exercised all due diligence to prevent the commission of the
-- offence." The burden is on the director.
GIVEN `the body corporate is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was a director or officer at the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves it was without his knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves all due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the director is deemed guilty` IF
        `the body corporate is convicted`
    AND `was a director or officer at the time`
    AND (NOT `proves it was without his knowledge`)
    AND (NOT `proves all due diligence`)

§§ `16(6) -- acts of a partner, agent or servant`

-- s 16(6): a person is liable to the same penalty "if the thing has been done or omitted by his partner, agent or servant, unless he
-- proves to the satisfaction of the court that he took all reasonable precautions to prevent the doing or omission of the thing."
GIVEN `done or omitted by his partner, agent or servant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal is liable` IF
    `done or omitted by his partner, agent or servant` AND (NOT `proves all reasonable precautions`)
